# Task Completion Guidelines (`.did/.hooks/done`)

[TASK COMPLETION CHECKLIST]
Before completing a task, confirm that:
1. All functional requirements are 100% satisfied with zero open questions or remaining work.
2. Automated unit and integration tests are written and passing (`cargo test`).
3. Strict compiler linting passes without warnings (`cargo clippy -- -D warnings`).
4. Required test coverage thresholds are met (`cargo llvm-cov`).

[REMINDER] If this issue or task was NOT fully completed or if remaining work/bugs were discovered:
  1. Mark the issue undone: $ did undone <PATH>
  2. Move it back to refine/ with explicit clarifying questions: $ did mv <PATH> refine/<PATH>
